§§ `Everyone: reporting (ss 3, 17, 18)`

-- s 3: Graham's death at home is a Western Australian death; it is not reportable while expected, natural and certified; a
-- fall (injury), a lock-up (held in care) and no certificate (limb (i)) make it reportable.
#ASSERT `Is this death a Western Australian death` `as family` `Graham, expected` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this death a Western Australian death` `as a doctor present` `Graham, a fall` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this death a Western Australian death` `as someone else who knows` `Graham, lock-up` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is this a Western Australian death` `Graham, lock-up`)
#ASSERT `Is this death a reportable death` `as family` `Graham, expected` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is this death a reportable death` `as family` `Graham, a fall` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this death a reportable death` `as family` `Graham, uncertified` EQUALS `yes if` (`Is this a reportable death` `Graham, uncertified`)
#ASSERT `Is this death a reportable death` `as a doctor present` `Graham, uncertified` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is this death a reportable death` `as someone else who knows` `Graham, lock-up` EQUALS yes

