§§ `The family: the investigation, the inquest, the next of kin, the post mortem and the body`

#ASSERT `Will the coroner investigate this death` `as family` `Graham, expected` `no directions` FALSE EQUALS `the investigation` `no: it is not a reportable death, so the coroner has no jurisdiction (s 19(1))`
#ASSERT `Will the coroner investigate this death` `as family` `Graham, sudden, certified` `no directions` TRUE EQUALS `the investigation` `the coroner need not investigate: natural causes, reportable only because unexpected (s 19A)`
#ASSERT `Will the coroner investigate this death` `as family` `Graham, uncertified` `no directions` TRUE EQUALS `the investigation` `yes: the death must be investigated (ss 8(c), 19(1))`
#ASSERT `Will the coroner investigate this death` `as family` `Graham, a fall` `no directions` FALSE EQUALS `the investigation` (`Will the coroner investigate` `Graham, a fall` `no directions` FALSE)

#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held into this death` `as family` `Graham, expected` `no directions` EQUALS `the inquest` `no: the coroner has no jurisdiction, so there can be no inquest`
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held into this death` `as family` `Graham, lock-up` `no directions` EQUALS `the inquest` `yes: an inquest must be held (s 22(1) or s 23(2))`
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held into this death` `as family` `Graham, a fall` `no directions` EQUALS `the inquest` `only if the coroner thinks it desirable (s 22(2)); we may ask for one (s 24)`
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held into this death` `as family` `Graham, a fall` `an inquest directed by the State Coroner` EQUALS `the inquest` `yes: an inquest must be held (s 22(1) or s 23(2))`
#ASSERT `Must an inquest be held into this death` `as family` `Graham, uncertified` `no directions` EQUALS `the inquest` (`Must an inquest be held` `Graham, uncertified` `no directions`)

