#ASSERT `Does the coroner hold the body, or may we have it` `as family` `Graham, expected` FALSE EQUALS `the body` `not held by the coroner: the Coroners Act does not hold it back`
#ASSERT `Does the coroner hold the body, or may we have it` `as family` `Graham, a fall` FALSE EQUALS `the body` `held by the coroner until the s 29 certificate is issued (s 30(1))`
#ASSERT `Does the coroner hold the body, or may we have it` `as family` `Graham, uncertified` TRUE EQUALS `the body` `released: the s 29 certificate permits burial, cremation or other disposal`
#ASSERT `Does the coroner hold the body, or may we have it` `as family` `Graham, lock-up` FALSE EQUALS `the body` (`Does the coroner hold the body` `Graham, lock-up` FALSE)
#ASSERT `When can the coroner issue the certificate releasing the body` `as family` `a request was refused and the 2 clear working days to apply to the Supreme Court are running` EQUALS `the disposal certificate` `not yet: the s 36 application or the time for it must run out first (s 29(2))`
#ASSERT `When can the coroner issue the certificate releasing the body` `as family` `the Supreme Court has ordered a post mortem (s 36(4))` EQUALS `the disposal certificate` `only the State Coroner may issue it, after the ordered post mortem (ss 29(3), 36(4))`
#ASSERT `When can the coroner issue the certificate releasing the body` `as family` `no one's request for a post mortem has been refused` EQUALS `the disposal certificate` `now: the coroner must issue it as soon as reasonably possible (s 29(1))`
#ASSERT `When can the coroner issue the certificate releasing the body` `as family` `the time to apply has passed with no application` EQUALS `the disposal certificate` (`When can the disposal certificate issue` `the time to apply has passed with no application`)

